---
// 测评文章（Tom's Guide / Wirecutter 结构版）
// 结构：结论前置 → 推荐卡片 → 产品模块（规格表 + Reasons to buy/avoid + 叙述段）→ 落选机型 → 怎么挑 → 分流
// 写新测评 = 复制此文件改内容；数据必须来自真实来源（官网规格 / 具名实验室 / 买家反馈）
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Best Budget 4K TVs Under $500 — DealWillow"
  description="The best 4K TVs under $500 in the US right now: the TCL QM6K for most people, and the Vizio Mini LED Quantum if brightness matters more than polish."
>
  <main class="wrap article">
    <a class="crumb" href="/">&larr; All reviews</a>

    <div class="head">
      <span class="cat-tag">TVs</span>
      <h1>Best Budget 4K TVs Under $500</h1>
      <p class="meta">Updated Nov 2026 · Prices checked Nov 9, 2026 · US models only</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 结论前置：学 Wirecutter/Tom's Guide 的第一段 -->
    <div class="lede">
      <p>
        <strong>Our pick for most people is the TCL QM6K.</strong> It's the budget set that named review
        labs keep recommending, its spec sheet (144&nbsp;Hz, QD-Mini&nbsp;LED, four HDMI inputs) checks out
        on TCL's own site, and owner discussion around it is overwhelmingly positive. If pure brightness
        for the money matters more to you than polish, the <strong>Vizio Mini LED Quantum at $278</strong> is
        the other name worth knowing — with two real caveats below.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 快速推荐卡片 -->
    <h2 class="block-title">Everything we recommend</h2>
    <div class="picks">
      <a class="pick" href="#qm6k">
        <span class="pick-tag">Best overall</span>
        <span class="pick-role">The safest budget TV to buy right now</span>
        <span class="pick-name">TCL QM6K (55QM6K)</span>
        <span class="pick-price">~$500 for 55" · Amazon</span>
      </a>
      <a class="pick" href="#vizio">
        <span class="pick-tag alt">Brightest for the money</span>
        <span class="pick-role">Measurably brighter, with real trade-offs</span>
        <span class="pick-name">Vizio Mini LED Quantum (VQM55C)</span>
        <span class="pick-price">$278 for 55" · Walmart</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- ============ 产品一：TCL QM6K ============ -->
    <section class="product" id="qm6k">
      <h2 class="prod-role">Best overall</h2>
      <h3 class="prod-name">1. TCL QM6K</h3>

      <div class="specs">
        <div><span>Sizes</span><b>55" – 98"</b></div>
        <div><span>Panel</span><b>QD-Mini LED, up to LD500 dimming</b></div>
        <div><span>Refresh rate</span><b>144 Hz native, VRR up to 144 Hz</b></div>
        <div><span>HDR</span><b>HDR10, HDR10+, HLG, Dolby Vision</b></div>
        <div><span>HDMI</span><b>4 inputs (1 eARC)</b></div>
        <div><span>Smart OS</span><b>Google TV</b></div>
        <div><span>Warranty</span><b>1 year limited</b></div>
      </div>

      <div class="proscons">
        <div class="pros">
          <p class="pc-title">Reasons to buy</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Named lab testing puts it at or near the top of this price tier</li>
            <li>144&nbsp;Hz panel with VRR — genuinely useful for PS5 and PC gaming</li>
            <li>Google TV is fast and has the widest app support</li>
            <li>Owner sentiment is strongly positive (79% of 108 mentions analyzed)</li>
            <li>Street prices from $400–$530, all the way up to 98"</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cons">
          <p class="pc-title">Reasons to avoid</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Noticeable glare in bright, sun-facing rooms</li>
            <li>Motion blur shows up during fast sports</li>
            <li>~500 dimming zones leave visible blooming around subtitles</li>
            <li>Scattered owner reports of panel flicker and QC issues</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="body">
        <p>
          The QM6K is the entry point to TCL's QD-Mini LED lineup, and it's where most of the
          "budget TV tech" story actually pays off. TCL's own spec sheet lists a native 144&nbsp;Hz
          panel with variable refresh rate up to 144&nbsp;Hz, up to 500 local dimming zones, a
          Google TV platform, a 40&nbsp;W Onkyo 2.1 speaker system, and four HDMI inputs (one eARC) —
          the kind of connectivity that was flagship territory a few years ago. The one-year limited
          warranty is average for the class; the Costco version is frequently discussed by owners for
          its better matte finish.
        </p>
        <p>
          In independent testing, this is the set budget-TV guides keep coming back to. Wirecutter
          named the QM6K its runner-up pick in 2026, specifically calling out its fast, accurate local
          dimming and "consistently inky and immersive shadow tones," while noting it's meaningfully
          less bright than the Vizio below — roughly 600 nits versus ~1,000. If your room is dark and
          you care about contrast more than peak brightness, that trade favors the TCL.
        </p>
        <p>
          Owner feedback lines up with the reviews. Across 108 Reddit mentions analyzed in September
          2026, sentiment is 79% positive: people praise movie and HDR picture quality, the value at
          larger sizes, and brightness that holds up in normal living rooms. The recurring complaints
          are consistent too — glare in bright rooms, color washing out at side angles, blur during
          football and soccer, and halo around bright subtitles on dark scenes. A smaller group of
          owners report quality-control issues like panel banding or flickering when local contrast is
          enabled; those reports are real but appear to affect a minority of units, and no major review
          lab has documented the issue across samples.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The bottom line:</strong> if you watch movies and play games in a room where you can
          control the light, this is the budget TV to buy. If your living room is a greenhouse at
          2&nbsp;p.m., see below.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 产品二：Vizio ============ -->
    <section class="product" id="vizio">
      <h2 class="prod-role">Brightest for the money</h2>
      <h3 class="prod-name">2. Vizio Mini LED Quantum</h3>

      <div class="specs">
        <div><span>Sizes</span><b>43" – 85"</b></div>
        <div><span>Panel</span><b>Mini-LED, full-array local dimming, quantum dots</b></div>
        <div><span>Refresh rate</span><b>60 Hz (1080p at 120 Hz)</b></div>
        <div><span>HDR</span><b>HDR10, HDR10+, HLG, Dolby Vision</b></div>
        <div><span>HDMI</span><b>3 inputs (1 eARC)</b></div>
        <div><span>Smart OS</span><b>Vizio OS (Walmart account required)</b></div>
        <div><span>Where to buy</span><b>Walmart &amp; Sam's Club only</b></div>
      </div>

      <div class="proscons">
        <div class="pros">
          <p class="pc-title">Reasons to buy</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Measured ~1,000 nits in independent testing — rare under $300</li>
            <li>Full HDR format support including Dolby Vision</li>
            <li>Low input lag for the price</li>
            <li>55-inch for $278, with a $248 deal price seen in November</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cons">
          <p class="pc-title">Reasons to avoid</p>
          <ul>
            <li>60&nbsp;Hz panel limits 4K gaming to 60&nbsp;fps</li>
            <li>Requires a Walmart account for smart features — a privacy trade</li>
            <li>Build and sound quality are visibly budget</li>
            <li>Some coverage disputes its black levels and processing</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="body">
        <p>
          The Mini LED Quantum is Vizio's return to the budget fight, and on paper it's almost
          absurd: mini-LED backlighting, quantum dots, full-array local dimming, Dolby Vision, and
          three HDMI inputs — from $278 for 55 inches. Wirecutter measured around 1,000 nits of peak
          brightness on the 75-inch version, which is double what most sets in this bracket manage,
          and made it their top budget pick for exactly that reason. In a bright, daytime living room,
          that number is the whole argument.
        </p>
        <p>
          But this is the set where our sources disagree most, so we'll be straight with you. Other
          coverage citing RTINGS measurements describes weak black levels, visible blooming, and
          middling picture processing, ranking it behind pricier rivals — and that coverage even
          conflicts with English-language sources on whether the HDMI ports are 2.1 or 2.0. Two
          credible picture-quality stories, two different conclusions. Until the exact US model's
          RTINGS numbers are checked directly, treat the Vizio's processing as an open question and
          buy it for brightness, not for polish.
        </p>
        <p>
          The other caveat isn't about picture at all: Vizio's smart platform wants a Walmart account
          for streaming features, and it has drawn years of complaints for ads and sluggishness. Many
          owners simply plug in a streaming stick and ignore the built-in OS entirely — which works,
          and sidesteps the issue.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The bottom line:</strong> buy it if brightness-per-dollar is your priority and you
          accept a 60&nbsp;Hz panel. If you game at 4K/120 or hate ad-heavy interfaces, pay the extra
          for the TCL.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 落选机型：学 Tom's Guide 的 "didn't quite make the cut" -->
    <section class="sec">
      <h2 class="block-title">Also worth knowing</h2>
      <p>
        Two more names come up consistently in 2026 roundups: the <strong>Hisense U6/Q65QF</strong> line,
        repeatedly cited as the brightest HDR alternative under $500 (with more blooming and a weaker
        Fire TV interface, per those same roundups), and the <strong>TCL Q6</strong>, the simpler QLED
        that's the easy choice if the QM6K is over budget. We haven't cross-checked either against
        primary lab data yet, so treat them as leads — we'll write them up properly when we have.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 怎么挑：轻量方法说明 -->
    <section class="sec">
      <h2 class="block-title">How we picked</h2>
      <p>
        We started from the sets that named testing labs (Wirecutter, RTINGS) actually recommend in
        this price bracket, then verified every spec against the manufacturer's own US product page —
        size, panel type, refresh rate, HDMI count, warranty. Anything that only existed in marketing
        copy got dropped. Then we read what owners say: 108 Reddit mentions for the TCL, retailer
        discussion threads for the Vizio, looking for problems that repeat across many buyers rather
        than one-off complaints. Prices were checked on <strong>Nov 9, 2026</strong> and will move —
        holiday sales especially.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 谁该跳过 -->
    <section class="sec">
      <h2 class="block-title">Who should skip this price tier</h2>
      <p>
        If your room gets heavy daytime sun, you watch mostly live sports, or you want uncompromised
        4K/120&nbsp;Hz gaming, the sub-$500 tier will frustrate you in some way — every set here trades
        away brightness headroom, motion handling, or QC polish. The $700–$900 mini-LED tier is where
        those complaints mostly fade, according to every roundup we read. That's a consistent pattern
        across sources, not a measurement of ours.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 收尾分流 -->
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .article { max-width: 780px; padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 30px; }
  .crumb { font-size: 13.5px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }

  .head { margin-top: 14px; }
  .cat-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 800;
    color: #1e66f5; background: #e0ecff;
    padding: 3px 10px; border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .article h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 31px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.5px; line-height: 1.15; }
  .meta { margin: 2px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }

  /* 结论前置段 */
  .lede { margin-top: 20px; }
  .lede p { margin: 0; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.7; color: #1f2937; }

  /* 区块标题 */
  .block-title { margin: 34px 0 14px; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.3px; }

  /* 快速推荐卡片 */
  .picks { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; }
  .pick {
    display: block;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, transform 0.15s ease;
  }
  .pick:hover { border-color: var(--blue); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .pick-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 800;
    color: #1d4ed8; background: #dbeafe;
    padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .pick-tag.alt { color: #b45309; background: #fef3c7; }
  .pick-role { display: block; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 3px; }
  .pick-name { display: block; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .pick-price { display: block; font-size: 13px; color: #374151; }

  /* 产品模块 */
  .product { margin-top: 40px; }
  .prod-role {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 800;
    color: #1d4ed8; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .prod-name { margin: 2px 0 14px; font-size: 26px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.4px; }

  /* 规格表：两列网格 */
  .specs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
  }
  .specs div {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .specs div:nth-child(2n) { border-right: none; }

  .specs span { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; }
  .specs b { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }

  /* 优缺点双栏 */
  .proscons { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; margin: 16px 0 4px; }
  .pros, .cons { border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; }
  .pros { background: #f0fdf4; border: 1px solid #bbf7d0; }
  .cons { background: #fef2f2; border: 1px solid #fecaca; }
  .pc-title { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 13.5px; font-weight: 800; }
  .pros .pc-title { color: #15803d; }
  .cons .pc-title { color: #b91c1c; }
  .pros ul, .cons ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; }
  .pros li, .cons li { font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: #1f2937; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .pros li:last-child, .cons li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* 正文 */
  .body { margin-top: 18px; }
  .body p { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.75; color: #1f2937; }

  .sec { margin-top: 32px; }
  .sec p { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.75; color: #1f2937; }
  .ending { padding-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .disclose-line { font-size: 12.5px !important; color: var(--muted) !important; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .article h1 { font-size: 25px; }
    .prod-name { font-size: 22px; }
    .picks, .proscons { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .specs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .specs div { border-right: none; }
  }
</style>
